        'Japan',
      ],
      timeline: [
        'Traditional period: Sevens-style layout play circulates in Japan under the name Shichi Narabe.',
        'Modern era: Variant families (Joker, Tunnel, Ghost, Killing) become widely documented.',
        'Current era: Online implementations spread standardized and house-rule versions.',
      ],
      evolution: 'Japanese rules introduced pass-economy pressure and special variants that punish blocking more strongly than many Western Sevens forms.',
